 \"What sport is Bragin associated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"sport\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 109, \"text\": \"Lyudmila Bragina Lyudmila Ivanovna Bragina (, born 24 July 1943) is a retired Russian middle distance runner.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d00\", \"start\": 110, \"end\": 242, \"text\": \"She competed for the Soviet Union in the 1500 m at the 1972 and 1976 Olympics; she won the event in 1972 and finished fifth in 1976.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d00\", \"start\": 243, \"end\": 460, \"text\": \"In July 1972 she set a new 1500 m world record of 4:06.9, at the Soviet championships, and then progressively improved it in round 1 (4:06.47), the semi-finals (4:05.07}, and the final (4:01.38), of the 1972 Olympics.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d00\", \"start\": 461, \"end\": 529, \"text\": \"The same year she was awarded the Order of the Red Banner of Labour.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d00\", \"start\": 530, \"end\": 554, \"text\": \"She also set three world\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 104, \"text\": \"Lyudmila Bragina Lyudmila Ivanovna Bragina (, born 24 July 1943) is a retired Russian ice hockey player.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d01\", \"start\": 105, \"end\": 237, \"text\": \"She competed for the Soviet Union in the 1500 m at the 1972 and 1976 Olympics; she won the event in 1972 and finished fifth in 1976.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d01\", \"start\": 238, \"end\": 455, \"text\": \"In July 1972 she set a new 1500 m world record of 4:06.9, at the Soviet championships, and then progressively improved it in round 1 (4:06.47), the semi-finals (4:05.07), and the final (4:01.38), of the 1972 Olympics.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d01\", \"start\": 456, \"end\": 524, \"text\": \"The same year she was awarded the Order of the Red Banner of Labour.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d01\", \"start\": 525, \"end\": 572, \"text\": \"She also set three world records in ice hockey.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 104, \"text\": \"Valeri Bragin Valeri Nikolayevich Bragin (); born May 31, 1956, is a retired Russian ice hockey forward.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 105, \"end\": 162, \"text\": \"He is former coach of the HC CSKA Moscow team in the KHL.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 163, \"end\": 270, \"text\": \"Valeri Bragin started his career with HC Spartak Moscow where he played in the top Soviet league from 1978.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 271, \"end\": 338, \"text\": \"In 1981 he joined Khimik Voskresensk where he played for 8 seasons.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 339, \"end\": 438, \"text\": \"In 1989 Bragin moved to Denmark where he was the player/coach for Rødovre SIK in the Danish League.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 439, \"end\": 484, \"text\": \"He won the Danish title with Rødovre in 1990.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0172-b91092d330d1:d02\", \"start\": 485, \"end\": 544, \"text\": \"In that season he was also named league player of the year.\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-017